I've been thinking recently that nethack should have real levels.  For
example, maybe the first ten floors being based on the ancient past,
another set of floors for a medievel world, SF settings, Alice in
Wonderland, OZ, etc.  In order to keep players on their toes,
different weapons should work on the different levels.  This way, PC's
can't accumulate a massive sword, armor, etc., they have to every so
often discard what they have and get something else unless they can
carry 10 different swords and such.  Gods and such might not work in a
technological setting.  Due to space limitations on micros and such,
each different group of levels could be a different program.  Finally,
which set of floors you get shouldn't be static, but should be random,
like most of nethack already is.

The level concept could be something like a transporter, where you
don't get to keep your items.  It could also be a series of subquests,
where the transporter doesn't work until you have the special
do-hickey for this subquest (say, the magic foot creme of Oz).

